Dear Priya,

Thank you for your e-mail of 21 February and the Levantina report.

Brisamar does not accept that the Bay 3 slab is outside tolerance. The slab w=
as surveyed by the main contractor on completion in August 2024 and found to =
be within 5 mm over 3 m. We will send that survey to you when we have it from=
 the main contractor. In the meantime we do not accept CO-3 and we do not acc=
ept any extension of time on this ground.

Tidewell's supports are, as you say, adjustable, and Tidewell's tender confir=
med that minor deviations could be accommodated. Please proceed with the inst=
allation at Tidewell's risk. If Tidewell considers that local grouting is req=
uired it should carry this out as part of its installation works.

Please send your cost and time proposal in any event so that we have it on fi=
le, but you should not treat this as an instruction.

Regarding the power supply, Marc is chasing the utility and will revert.

Best regards,

